  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration is config_030 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.632 acc / 0.607 F1. We have strong evidence that (a) multimodal > unimodal, (b) multiprofile + avgpool > singleprofile or transformer, and (c) scvi_n200 ≥ pca_n2000. However, the image encoder has only been tested as resnet50, which produced a very weak image-only baseline (0.208). The imagenet_vit_l encoder is completely untested and represents the largest remaining unexplored design axis. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l improve multimodal performance when paired with the best-known RNA encoder (scvi_n200) and aggregation (avgpool)? Why this is the best next experiment: config_036 isolates the image-encoder change while holding all other components at their empirically validated best values, directly extending the current champion. A positive result would identify a new promising direction and justify further exploration (weighted fusion, transformer aggregation with VIT-L); a null or negative result would efficiently rule out an entire family of 8+ configurations, saving budget. No other single experiment reduces as much uncertainty about a high-impact design choice."
}

